# Code conventions

## Context

`app/` is TypeScript strict (`noUncheckedIndexedAccess` on) and ESM
(`"type": "module"`). Existing files — `app/src/actions.ts`,
`app/src/selectors.ts`, `app/src/lib/text.ts` — all follow the same shape:
named exports, explicit types, relative imports ending in `.js`. New code must
be indistinguishable from it.

## Rule

- Named exports only. NEVER use `export default`.
- NEVER use `any`, `as any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, or
  non-null-assertion `!` to silence the compiler. With
  `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, handle `undefined` from index access explicitly
  (`tasks[0]?.done`, or a guard).
- Immutable updates only: spread, `map`, `filter`, `concat`. NEVER `push`,
  `splice`, `sort`, or direct property assignment on state.
- Relative imports MUST use the `.js` extension (`from "./types.js"`), and
  type-only imports use `import type { ... }`.
- File names are kebab-case (`text.ts`, `task-utils.ts`); types/interfaces are
  PascalCase; functions/variables camelCase; action `type` strings use the
  `domain/event` form (`"task/added"`).
- Every exported function has explicit parameter and return types.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rn "export default" app/src` → zero matches.
2. `grep -rnE ":\s*any\b|as any|@ts-ignore|@ts-expect-error" app/src` → zero
   matches.
3. `grep -rnE "from \"\./[^\"]*\"" app/src | grep -v "\.js\"" ` → zero matches
   (all relative imports carry `.js`).
4. `ls app/src app/src/lib` → every filename is lower-case kebab-case.
5. `cd app && npm run typecheck` → no errors (no suppressions used).

